        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and use [[def-qft-dirac-projections]] and [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]]. Define $\\chi(s)=\\cos s+i\\sin s$ for real $s$, using [[def-sine-and-cosine-by-power-series]]. Let $X=(\\{+\\}\\times\\mathbb R^3)\\sqcup(\\{-\\}\\times\\mathbb R^3)$ carry counting measure on the species label and $d^3\\mathbf k/(2\\pi)^3$ on each copy. The fiber $\\mathcal V_x$ is $\\mathbb C^4$ for $x=(+,\\mathbf k)$ and $\\overline{\\mathbb C^4}$ for $x=(-,\\mathbf k)$; $L^2(X;\\mathcal V)$ denotes measurable sections with square-integrable fiber norm, and is the direct sum $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C^4)\\oplus L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\overline{\\mathbb C^4})$. Identify $\\mathcal K=\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-}$ with the closed subspace whose $+$ fibers lie in $\\operatorname{ran}P_+(\\mathbf k)$ and whose $-$ fibers lie in $\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}P_-(\\mathbf k)}$; form its antisymmetric Fock space $\\mathcal F_a(\\mathcal K)$ using [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. For $x=(+,\\mathbf k)$ set $q(x)=(\\omega(\\mathbf k),\\mathbf k)$, and for $x=(-,\\mathbf k)$ set $q(x)=(\\omega(\\mathbf k),-\\mathbf k)$. The one-particle translation multipliers $V(a)u(x)=\\chi(q^0(x)a^0-\\mathbf q(x)\\cdot\\mathbf a)u(x)$ preserve $\\mathcal K$ and lift to a strongly continuous unitary representation on $\\mathcal F_a(\\mathcal K)$. Write $U_j(t)$ for its Fock lift along the $j$th coordinate axis of $\\mathbb R^4$.\n\nOn the $n$-particle sector, let $s_n(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)=\\sum_{r=1}^n q(x_r)$ and set $s_0=0$ on the vacuum sector. The joint spectral measure is multiplication by $\\mathbf1_{s_n^{-1}(B)}$ on each sector, restricted to its antisymmetric subspace. Its support is contained in the closed future cone $\\{(E,\\mathbf p):E\\ge|\\mathbf p|\\}$. Define the time generator $H$ and spatial momentum components $P_j$ by $U(te_0)=\\chi(tH)$ and $U(te_j)=\\chi(-tP_j)$, where $e_\\alpha$ are the coordinate vectors in translation space. Then $H$ and each $P_j$ are the maximal real multipliers by $s_{n,0}$ and $s_{n,j}$, respectively, with domains $\\{\\Psi:\\sum_n\\|s_{n,\\alpha}\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\}$; the minus sign in spatial translation phases is the Minkowski pairing convention in $V(a)$. The vacuum is the unique zero-energy vector; for $\\mu>0$ the nonvacuum spectrum has gap at least $\\mu$, while for $\\mu=0$ it has no positive gap.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 5, quantizing the Dirac field",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qft.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 155-page author-hosted notes; Chapter 5 §§5.2–5.4, fermionic modes, antiparticles, and positive-energy Fock interpretation."
            },
            {
              "title": "Niklas Beisert, Quantum Field Theory I, ETH Zürich 2025 HS complete lecture notes",
              "url": "https://people.phys.ethz.ch/~nbeisert/lectures/QFT1-25HS-Notes.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 194-page official course notes; Chapter 5 §§5.1, 5.2, 5.4–5.6, printed 5.1–5.6 and 5.10–5.18, for Clifford algebra, spinor covariance, Hamiltonian form and fermionic quantization. The exact local conventions and domains are proved in the library."
            }
          ]
        }
