        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and the mathematical free Dirac data of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]], [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]], and [[lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality]]. Let $G=\\mathbb R^4\\rtimes SO^+(1,3)$ act by $x\\mapsto a+\\Lambda x$, with product $(a_2,\\Lambda_2)(a_1,\\Lambda_1)=(a_2+\\Lambda_2a_1,\\Lambda_2\\Lambda_1)$. Let $\\widetilde G$ be the subgroup of triples $(a,\\Lambda,S)$ generated by translations $(a,I,I)$ and the explicit rotation/boost triples $(0,R_{\\mathbf n}(\\theta),S_R(\\theta))$ and $(0,B_{\\mathbf n}(\\chi),S_B(\\chi))$ of [[lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices]], with product $(a_2,\\Lambda_2,S_2)(a_1,\\Lambda_1,S_1)=(a_2+\\Lambda_2a_1,\\Lambda_2\\Lambda_1,S_2S_1)$ and the subspace topology from $\\mathbb R^4\\times M_4(\\mathbb R)\\times GL(4,\\mathbb C)$. Its projection onto $G$ is surjective by [[lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization]]. For $\\tilde g=(a,\\Lambda,S)$ define the spinor test pullback\n$$\\tau_{\\tilde g}F(x)=(S^{-1})^\\dagger F(\\Lambda^{-1}(x-a)).$$\nThe fermionic Fock space of [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]] carries a strongly continuous unitary representation $U$ of $\\widetilde G$ such that\n$$U(\\tilde g)\\Psi(F)U(\\tilde g)^{-1}=\\Psi(\\tau_{\\tilde g}F).$$\nLet $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{gr}}$ be the algebra generated by all bounded $\\Psi(F)$ and $\\Psi(F)^\\dagger$ for Schwartz spinor tests $F$. The vacuum $\\Omega$ is invariant and cyclic for $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{gr}}$. A $2\\pi$ spatial spin rotation acts as $(-1)^N$ on the $n$-particle sector with value $(-1)^n$; a $4\\pi$ rotation acts as the identity. The translation generators and joint spectral measure are those of [[lem-qft-dirac-fermionic-translation-spectrum]], so the joint spectrum is contained in the closed future cone, $\\Omega$ is the unique zero-energy vector, and for $\\mu>0$ the nonvacuum energy has gap at least $\\mu$. The first-quantized $h_D$ has both signs of energy; this Fock-space generator is a different operator on a different Hilbert space. No general spin-statistics theorem or local cyclicity claim is asserted.",
