        "dependency_level": 3,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "statement": "Take the fiber matrices of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]] at $\\mathbf k=0$ with $\\mu>0$. Then $\\omega=\\mu$ and the positive and negative matrix eigenspaces each have dimension two. The coordinate spinors displayed below are vectors in the finite-dimensional fiber $\\mathbb C^4$; they are not point-supported, normalizable vectors in the continuum Hilbert space $\\mathcal H_D$. For $\\mu=0$, the point $(\\omega,\\mathbf k)=(0,0)$ is the omitted mass-shell apex, so this example makes no massless rest-state claim.",
